00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.533
What's the good news, Wes?

00:01:43.533 --> 00:01:44.950
WESLEY CHUN: Well,
Cloud Datastore

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:46.910
became its own product in 2013.

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:48.960
But the following
year, Google acquired

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:51.900
Firebase for its amazing
realtime database.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.270
Both teams then worked
together and launched

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:58.410
the next-generation scalable
NoSQL database in 2017.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:01.080
To show that Datastore
joined forces with Firebase,

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.055
the product was rebranded
as Cloud Firestore.

00:02:04.055 --> 00:02:05.430
MARTIN OMANDER:
Oh, yeah, and you

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:08.020
told me to wait until
this video to learn more.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.510
So here we are.

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:11.250
You also mentioned
that Firestore

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.170
