00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:12.010
You have to have a new project.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:14.730
So once again, you really
need to have a good reason

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.360
to make this migration.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:19.839
And if accessing those Firebase
features is compelling enough,

00:04:19.839 --> 00:04:21.990
you got to do what
you got to do, right?

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:23.820
MARTIN OMANDER:
Yeah, that's right.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:26.290
Well, I do want to take
advantage of Firestore's

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:28.710
native features, and I'm
willing to create a new project

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:30.370
to make it happen.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.245
How do I get started?

00:04:31.245 --> 00:04:32.662
WESLEY CHUN: Well,
the first thing

00:04:32.662 --> 00:04:35.550
is you must recognize that there
are two pieces to this puzzle.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:37.560
First, your data
must be transferred

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:39.480
